# django-adminflow

**A premium, modern SaaS design system for the Django Admin interface.**

[![PyPI version](https://img.shields.io/pypi/v/django-adminflow.svg)](https://pypi.org/project/django-adminflow/)
[![Python versions](https://img.shields.io/pypi/pyversions/django-adminflow.svg)](https://pypi.org/project/django-adminflow/)
[![Django versions](https://img.shields.io/pypi/djversions/django-adminflow.svg)](https://pypi.org/project/django-adminflow/)
[![License: MIT](https://img.shields.io/badge/License-MIT-blue.svg)](LICENSE)

AdminFlow replaces the default Django admin skin with a clean, minimalist SaaS design system — dark mode ready, responsive, and production-hardened. Drop it into any Django project with minimal configuration.

---

## Features

| Feature | Description |
|---|---|
| 🎨 **Modern UI** | Minimalist SaaS design — clean typography, subtle shadows, responsive layout |
| 🔒 **Two-Factor Auth** | TOTP (Google/Authy), email OTP, and backup codes — add multiple devices |
| 📜 **Audit History** | Per-record change history with delta diffs, powered by `django-simple-history` |
| 📤 **Import / Export** | Multi-sheet XLSX and nested JSON export with related models in one file |
| 🔌 **Plug & Play** | One `INSTALLED_APPS` entry — no boilerplate required |
| 🌐 **i18n Ready** | All UI strings wrapped in `{% translate %}` |

---

## Installation

### Minimal (UI only)

```bash
pip install django-adminflow
```

### With 2FA support

```bash
pip install "django-adminflow[otp]"
```

### With audit history

```bash
pip install "django-adminflow[history]"
```

### With import / export

```bash
pip install "django-adminflow[import-export]"
```

### Everything

```bash
pip install "django-adminflow[all]"
```

---

## Quick Setup

### 1. `settings.py`

```python
INSTALLED_APPS = [
    "adminflow",          # must come BEFORE django.contrib.admin
    "django.contrib.admin",
    "django.contrib.auth",
    "django.contrib.contenttypes",
    "django.contrib.sessions",
    "django.contrib.messages",
    "django.contrib.staticfiles",

    # Optional: add only the ones you installed
    "simple_history",
    "import_export",
    "django_otp",
    "django_otp.plugins.otp_totp",
    "django_otp.plugins.otp_email",
    "django_otp.plugins.otp_static",
]

# Optional: customize the admin title
ADMINFLOW_TITLE = "My App"

MIDDLEWARE = [
    ...
    "django.contrib.auth.middleware.AuthenticationMiddleware",
    "django_otp.middleware.OTPMiddleware",
    ...
    "simple_history.middleware.HistoryRequestMiddleware",
]
```

---

## 3rd Party Integrations

AdminFlow has built-in support for the following packages. Each is **optional**.

### 🔒 Two-Factor Authentication — `django-otp`

```bash
pip install "django-adminflow[otp]"
```

What AdminFlow adds:
- OTP verification screen on login (TOTP / email)
- Per-device 2FA management in the user admin
- Add multiple authenticator apps or devices per user
- Backup codes (static OTP) generation
- Admin actions: *Enable 2FA*, *Generate 10 backup codes*

```python
# admin.py — minimal setup
from adminflow.user_admin import AdminFlowUserAdminMixin, get_2fa_inlines, unregister_otp_models
from django.contrib.auth.admin import UserAdmin as BaseUserAdmin

@admin.register(User)
class UserAdmin(AdminFlowUserAdminMixin, BaseUserAdmin):
    inlines = get_2fa_inlines()

unregister_otp_models()
```

---

### 📜 Audit History — `django-simple-history`

```bash
pip install "django-adminflow[history]"
```

What AdminFlow adds:
- Styled history list with delta diff highlighting
- Related model history merged into parent history view

```python
# models.py
from simple_history.models import HistoricalRecords

class Product(models.Model):
    name = models.CharField(max_length=200)
    history = HistoricalRecords()

# admin.py
from simple_history.admin import SimpleHistoryAdmin

@admin.register(Product)
class ProductAdmin(SimpleHistoryAdmin):
    ...
```

---

### 📤 Import / Export — `django-import-export`

```bash
pip install "django-adminflow[import-export]"
```

Add `import_export` to `INSTALLED_APPS`.

Export formats:

| Format | Output |
|---|---|
| **XLSX** | One `.xlsx` file — one sheet per related model |
| **JSON** | One `.json` file — child records nested inside parent records |

```python
# resources.py
from import_export import resources, fields
from import_export.widgets import ForeignKeyWidget
from .models import Customer, Order

class CustomerResource(resources.ModelResource):
    class Meta:
        model = Customer
        fields = ('id', 'name', 'email', 'phone', 'notes', 'date_created')

class OrderResource(resources.ModelResource):
    customer = fields.Field(
        column_name='customer_email',
        attribute='customer',
        widget=ForeignKeyWidget(Customer, field='email'),
    )
    class Meta:
        model = Order
        fields = ('id', 'customer', 'product', 'order_date', 'status', 'total_amount')

# admin.py
from adminflow.import_export import MultiSheetExportImportMixin
from import_export.admin import ImportExportModelAdmin

@admin.register(Customer)
class CustomerAdmin(MultiSheetExportImportMixin, ImportExportModelAdmin, admin.ModelAdmin):
    combined_sheets = [
        ('General Details', CustomerResource, None),
        ('Orders', OrderResource, lambda qs: Order.objects.filter(customer__in=qs)),
    ]
```

JSON output structure:

```json
[
  {
    "id": "1",
    "name": "Rooney Hutchinson",
    "email": "rooney@example.com",
    "orders": [
      {
        "id": "1",
        "customer_email": "rooney@example.com",
        "order_date": "2026-07-22",
        "status": "delivered",
        "total_amount": "42222.00"
      }
    ]
  }
]
```

---

## Admin Customisation

```python
# settings.py
ADMINFLOW_TITLE = "My SaaS App"
```

```python
# admin.py — custom Material Symbols icon
@admin.register(Product)
class ProductAdmin(admin.ModelAdmin):
    icon = "inventory_2"
```

---

## Changelog

### v1.0.0 — 2026-07-23

- Initial stable release
- Modern SaaS admin UI (minimalist, responsive)
- Full 2FA: TOTP, email OTP, backup codes, multi-device support
- Audit history with delta diffs (django-simple-history)
- Multi-sheet XLSX export/import (one sheet per related model)
- Nested JSON export (children embedded inside parent records)
- `MultiSheetExportImportMixin` for plug-and-play multi-resource export
- Styled Import / Export buttons and export page

---

## Publishing to PyPI

```bash
pip install build twine

# Build
cd "AdminFlow Package"
python -m build

# Upload
twine upload dist/*
```

